    <div class="market-activity-divider h-px [background:var(--surface-subtle)] [margin:28px_0] [transition:background_0.3s] dark:[background:rgb(var(--surface))]"></div>
    <div class="market-activity-section [margin:32px_0] [&_p]:[font-size:15px] [&_p]:[color:var(--text-secondary-strong)] [&_p]:[margin-bottom:10px] [&_p]:[transition:color_0.3s] [&_li]:[font-size:15px] [&_li]:[color:var(--text-secondary-strong)] [&_li]:[margin-bottom:10px] [&_li]:[transition:color_0.3s] dark:[&_p]:[color:rgb(var(--text-soft))] dark:[&_li]:[color:rgb(var(--text-soft))] [&_strong]:[color:rgb(var(--text-main))] [&_strong]:[font-weight:600] [&_strong]:[transition:color_0.3s] dark:[&_strong]:[color:var(--text-on-primary)]">
        <div class="market-activity-section-header flex items-center [gap:12px] [margin-bottom:18px] [padding-bottom:12px] [border-bottom:2px_solid_var(--border-subtle)] [transition:border-color_0.3s] dark:[border-bottom-color:rgb(var(--border))]">
            <span class="market-activity-section-number inline-flex items-center justify-center [width:36px] [height:36px] [border-radius:10px] [background:linear-gradient(135deg,_var(--surface-heading),_var(--surface-primary))] text-white font-bold [font-size:15px] shrink-0">7</span>
            <span class="market-activity-section-title [font-size:22px] font-bold [color:rgb(var(--text-main))] [letter-spacing:-0.3px] [transition:color_0.3s] dark:[color:var(--text-on-primary)] [&_i]:[color:var(--text-danger-15)] [&_i]:[margin-right:8px] [&_i]:[font-size:20px] max-[768px]:[font-size:18px]"><i class="fas fa-lightbulb"></i> How to Use This Strategy Effectively?</span>
        </div>
        <p>Monitoring Pinnacle odds drops is a widely used technique among sports betting professionals. Here are four key reasons why this data is valuable:</p>

        <div class="market-activity-subsection [margin-bottom:24px] [padding-left:8px]">
            <div class="market-activity-subsection-title [font-size:16px] font-semibold [color:var(--text-brand-60)] [margin-bottom:10px] [transition:color_0.3s] dark:[color:rgb(var(--text-soft))]">7.1 Following Market Movement</div>
            <p>Pinnacle is known for accepting high limits and for not restricting professional players. When odds move sharply, it often reflects significant volume placed on a specific outcome. Observing these movements can help you understand where the market is heading, without assuming the cause is always professional money.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="market-activity-subsection [margin-bottom:24px] [padding-left:8px]">
            <div class="market-activity-subsection-title [font-size:16px] font-semibold [color:var(--text-brand-60)] [margin-bottom:10px] [transition:color_0.3s] dark:[color:rgb(var(--text-soft))]">7.2 Early Signals of New Information</div>
            <p>Sharp odds movements can sometimes precede publicly available news. Examples include:</p>
            <ul class="guide-list [&_li::before]:content-['▸'] list-none p-0 [margin:8px_0_14px] [&_li]:[padding:5px_0_5px_22px] [&_li]:[position:relative] [&_li]:[font-size:13px] [&_li::before]:[position:absolute] [&_li::before]:[left:4px] [&_li::before]:[color:rgb(var(--primary))] [&_li::before]:[font-weight:700] dark:[&_li::before]:[color:rgb(var(--primary))]">
                <li>Sudden injury or disqualification of a key player</li>
                <li>Internal team conflict or a coaching change</li>
                <li>Sharp change in motivation (e.g., if a competitor lost points)</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Pinnacle&#039;s algorithms and users tend to react quickly, which can give you an informational advantage — though not a guarantee of any outcome.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="market-activity-subsection [margin-bottom:24px] [padding-left:8px]">
            <div class="market-activity-subsection-title [font-size:16px] font-semibold [color:var(--text-brand-60)] [margin-bottom:10px] [transition:color_0.3s] dark:[color:rgb(var(--text-soft))]">7.3 Finding Potential Value</div>
            <p>This is the most practical benefit:</p>
            <ul class="guide-list [&_li::before]:content-['▸'] list-none p-0 [margin:8px_0_14px] [&_li]:[padding:5px_0_5px_22px] [&_li]:[position:relative] [&_li]:[font-size:13px] [&_li::before]:[position:absolute] [&_li::before]:[left:4px] [&_li::before]:[color:rgb(var(--primary))] [&_li::before]:[font-weight:700] dark:[&_li::before]:[color:rgb(var(--primary))]">
                <li>When Pinnacle odds drop (e.g., from 2.10 to 1.80), other, softer bookmakers are often slower to react</li>
                <li>You may find a local or less popular bookmaker where the old, higher odds (2.10) are still available</li>
                <li>This can allow you to place a bet at odds higher than the implied fair probability, which is the basis of CLV (Closing Line Value) strategies — though long-term profit is not guaranteed</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="market-activity-example-block my-3 max-w-full overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-neutral-5-4)] bg-[var(--surface-neutral-0-10)] p-4 font-mono text-[13px] leading-relaxed whitespace-pre-line text-[var(--text-secondary-strong)] dark:border-[rgb(var(--border))] dark:bg-[rgb(var(--bg))] dark:text-[rgb(var(--text-soft))]">
                Example: Pinnacle <span class="hl-red font-semibold text-[var(--text-danger-15)] dark:text-[rgb(var(--danger))]">2.10 → 1.80</span>
                Soft Bookmaker still <span class="hl-green font-semibold text-[var(--text-success-35)] dark:text-[rgb(var(--success))]">2.10</span>
                → <span class="hl-green font-semibold text-[var(--text-success-35)] dark:text-[rgb(var(--success))]">Potential Value</span> (relative to Pinnacle&#039;s fair price)
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="market-activity-subsection [margin-bottom:24px] [padding-left:8px]">
            <div class="market-activity-subsection-title [font-size:16px] font-semibold [color:var(--text-brand-60)] [margin-bottom:10px] [transition:color_0.3s] dark:[color:rgb(var(--text-soft))]">7.4 Market Anomalies</div>
            <p>In lower leagues or less popular sports, <strong>anomalous and sharp odds drops</strong> can sometimes indicate unusual market behavior or the presence of non-public information. If odds drop without any obvious reason, it may be a signal that something unexpected is happening in the market — it does not by itself confirm any specific cause.</p>
            <div class="market-activity-info-card [background:linear-gradient(135deg,_var(--surface-panel),_var(--surface-hover))] [border-left:4px_solid_var(--border-primary)] [border-radius:0_12px_12px_0] [padding:16px_20px] [margin:14px_0_18px] [transition:0.3s] dark:[background:linear-gradient(135deg,_rgb(var(--surface-soft)),_rgb(var(--surface-soft)))] dark:[border-left-color:rgb(var(--border))] [&_p]:[margin-bottom:6px]! [&_p]:[font-size:14px]! [&_.label]:[font-size:11px] [&_.label]:[font-weight:700] [&_.label]:[text-transform:uppercase] [&_.label]:[color:rgb(var(--primary))] [&_.label]:[letter-spacing:0.5px] [&_.label]:[margin-bottom:6px] dark:[&_.label]:[color:rgb(var(--primary))]">
                <div class="label">How BF Markets Helps</div>
                <p>BF Markets&#039; <strong>Pinnacle Odds Drops</strong> page monitors exactly this strategy. It automatically records Pinnacle odds drops, analyzes Betfair Exchange prices, and displays <strong>Edge %</strong> — allowing you to:</p>
                <ul class="guide-list [&_li::before]:content-['▸'] list-none p-0 [margin:8px_0_14px] [&_li]:[padding:5px_0_5px_22px] [&_li]:[position:relative] [&_li]:[font-size:13px] [&_li::before]:[position:absolute] [&_li::before]:[left:4px] [&_li::before]:[color:rgb(var(--primary))] [&_li::before]:[font-weight:700] dark:[&_li::before]:[color:rgb(var(--primary))]">
                    <li>Quickly see where the market is moving</li>
                    <li>Discover potential Value Bets by Edge %</li>
                    <li>Receive signals about anomalous drops</li>
                    <li>Get automated alerts on Telegram</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
