            <span class="market-activity-section-number inline-flex items-center justify-center [width:36px] [height:36px] [border-radius:10px] [background:linear-gradient(135deg,_var(--surface-heading),_var(--surface-primary))] text-white font-bold [font-size:15px] shrink-0">8</span>
            <span class="market-activity-section-title [font-size:22px] font-bold [color:rgb(var(--text-main))] [letter-spacing:-0.3px] [transition:color_0.3s] dark:[color:var(--text-on-primary)] [&_i]:[color:var(--text-danger-15)] [&_i]:[margin-right:8px] [&_i]:[font-size:20px] max-[768px]:[font-size:18px]"><i class="fas fa-flask"></i> Practical Examples</span>
        </div>
        <p>Below are illustrative examples of how the metrics on this page can be interpreted. They are simplified and intended for educational purposes only.</p>

        <div class="market-activity-subsection [margin-bottom:24px] [padding-left:8px]">
            <div class="market-activity-subsection-title [font-size:16px] font-semibold [color:var(--text-brand-60)] [margin-bottom:10px] [transition:color_0.3s] dark:[color:rgb(var(--text-soft))]">8.1 Example: A Pinnacle Odds Drop</div>
            <p>Suppose Pinnacle moves a moneyline price from <strong>2.20</strong> to <strong>1.95</strong>. The page displays:</p>
            <ul class="guide-list [&_li::before]:content-['▸'] list-none p-0 [margin:8px_0_14px] [&_li]:[padding:5px_0_5px_22px] [&_li]:[position:relative] [&_li]:[font-size:13px] [&_li::before]:[position:absolute] [&_li::before]:[left:4px] [&_li::before]:[color:rgb(var(--primary))] [&_li::before]:[font-weight:700] dark:[&_li::before]:[color:rgb(var(--primary))]">
                <li><strong>Drop %:</strong> approximately −11.4%</li>
                <li><strong>Pinnacle Odds:</strong> 2.20 → 1.95</li>
                <li><strong>NVP:</strong> an estimated fair price after removing margin (e.g., ~2.02)</li>
            </ul>
            <p>These values help you see how far the market has moved and where the fair price sits relative to the current price.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="market-activity-subsection [margin-bottom:24px] [padding-left:8px]">
            <div class="market-activity-subsection-title [font-size:16px] font-semibold [color:var(--text-brand-60)] [margin-bottom:10px] [transition:color_0.3s] dark:[color:rgb(var(--text-soft))]">8.2 Example: Comparing Pinnacle and Betfair</div>
            <p>Using the same outcome, suppose Betfair shows a Back price of <strong>2.14</strong>. The page calculates Betfair Edge as:</p>
            <div class="market-activity-example-block my-3 max-w-full overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-neutral-5-4)] bg-[var(--surface-neutral-0-10)] p-4 font-mono text-[13px] leading-relaxed whitespace-pre-line text-[var(--text-secondary-strong)] dark:border-[rgb(var(--border))] dark:bg-[rgb(var(--bg))] dark:text-[rgb(var(--text-soft))]">Betfair Edge = (2.14 / 2.02 - 1) × 100 ≈ <span class="hl-green font-semibold text-[var(--text-success-35)] dark:text-[rgb(var(--success))]">+5.9%</span></div>
            <p>A positive Edge % means the Betfair price is higher than the estimated fair price. This is a signal worth investigating, not a guarantee of profitability.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="market-activity-subsection [margin-bottom:24px] [padding-left:8px]">
            <div class="market-activity-subsection-title [font-size:16px] font-semibold [color:var(--text-brand-60)] [margin-bottom:10px] [transition:color_0.3s] dark:[color:rgb(var(--text-soft))]">8.3 Example: Grouped Alerts</div>
            <p>If the same match produces several alerts (e.g., different totals or handicaps), the page groups them under one card. The card header shows the match, sport, league, and the number of alerts. Expanding the card reveals each individual alert — this keeps the terminal organized when many markets move at once.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="market-activity-subsection [margin-bottom:24px] [padding-left:8px]">
            <div class="market-activity-subsection-title [font-size:16px] font-semibold [color:var(--text-brand-60)] [margin-bottom:10px] [transition:color_0.3s] dark:[color:rgb(var(--text-soft))]">8.4 Example: Using the Detail Overlay</div>
            <p>Clicking an alert opens a detail overlay containing:</p>
            <ul class="guide-list [&_li::before]:content-['▸'] list-none p-0 [margin:8px_0_14px] [&_li]:[padding:5px_0_5px_22px] [&_li]:[position:relative] [&_li]:[font-size:13px] [&_li::before]:[position:absolute] [&_li::before]:[left:4px] [&_li::before]:[color:rgb(var(--primary))] [&_li::before]:[font-weight:700] dark:[&_li::before]:[color:rgb(var(--primary))]">
                <li>Top block: Drop, Pinnacle price, NVP, Pinnacle Edge, Betfair Back/Lay, sizes, Betfair Edge, and time</li>
                <li>Full market table: all outcomes with Pinnacle, NVP, Betfair, and Edge values</li>
                <li>Recent alerts: the last five alerts for the same match</li>
            </ul>
            <p>This view lets you compare outcomes side by side and judge whether the movement is isolated or part of a broader market shift.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

